 "text": "Hello, how are you keeping these trying times? Try moving your mic a way from the wall, or using a different in room mirror that's wider at the top. Then try using your hand to block the mirror while you talk, and see if the echo goes away. That's the mirror part. Then try speaking from further away, or using your hand to block one wall at a time. Whichever way gives you a cleaner sound. Start by standing right in front of the mirror, and take notes of how much echo you hear. Then step back a little while keeping the mirror in front of you. Good plan. mirror helps, so practice mirror techniques.",
